(meta r-ready-fix-blocking
  (description "Issue 1 (CRITICAL): Fix is_blocked_by_superior to block defeasible attackers when no superiority exists. Current code at reason.rs:364 only blocks when attacker_superior && !rule_superior. Must change to: block UNLESS rule > attacker (matching defeater logic). This is the defining property of SDL — without it, every unsuperior conflict produces inconsistent +d q AND +d ~q.")
  (priority "critical")
  (file "crates/spindle-core/src/reason.rs")
  (lines "354-371"))

(meta r-ready-unify-attacker
  (description "Issue 2 (MODERATE): Unify blocking logic for defeaters and defeasible attackers. Currently defeaters block unless rule > defeater (correct), but defeasible attackers block only if attacker > rule (wrong). Both should use the same condition from spec condition (3): block unless there exists t in Rsd[q] with t applicable AND t > s.")
  (priority "moderate")
  (file "crates/spindle-core/src/reason.rs")
  (lines "336-371"))

(meta r-ready-update-tests
  (description "Update test_mutual_non_superiority_allows_both_conclusions (line 893) to expect NEITHER +d q NOR +d ~q (ambiguity blocking). Add tests for the spec worked example: >> p, >> -p should yield -d p, -d -p. Review all existing tests for conformance with the new blocking semantics.")
  (priority "critical")
  (file "crates/spindle-core/src/reason.rs")
  (lines "893-923"))

(meta r-ready-spec-tests
  (description "Add comprehensive spec compliance tests: (1) conflicting defeasible rules without superiority, (2) conflicting defeasible rules WITH superiority resolving, (3) defeater blocks without proving, (4) defeater overridden by superior rule, (5) strict chain blocks defeasible, (6) cascading chains, (7) the worked example from the spec verbatim.")
  (priority "high"))

(meta r-ready-two-phase
  (description "Issue 3 (MODERATE): Separate definite and defeasible computation into two distinct phases. Phase 1 computes ALL +D/-D using only strict rules. Phase 2 uses complete definite results for defeasible reasoning. Current single-pass can derive +d p before discovering +D -p through a multi-hop strict chain.")
  (priority "moderate")
  (file "crates/spindle-core/src/reason.rs")
  (lines "110-288"))

(meta r-ready-neg-prop
  (description "Issue 4 (MODERATE): Implement negative conclusion propagation during defeasible reasoning. When a literal is proved -d, propagate it: discard rules with that literal in body, and try to prove the complement. Currently negatives are only computed as a passive sweep in Phase 3.")
  (priority "moderate")
  (file "crates/spindle-core/src/reason.rs")
  (lines "290-303"))

(meta r-ready-check-rsd
  (description "Issue 5 (MINOR): Expand is_blocked_by_superior to check ALL applicable Rsd[q] rules, not just the single rule being fired. Spec condition (3) says there exists ANY t in Rsd[q] with t > s. Current code only checks the triggering rule.")
  (priority "minor")
  (file "crates/spindle-core/src/reason.rs")
  (lines "309-374"))

(meta r-ready-fact-class
  (description "Issue 6 (SPEC INCONSISTENCY): Resolve contradiction in the spec. Rule type table says facts are Defeasible level, pseudocode seeds them as +D, worked example treats them as not +D. Decide which interpretation to follow and align both spec and implementation.")
  (priority "low"))

